Template: homelab-api-backend-processor/db/reuse_api_config
Type: boolean
Default: true
Description: Reuse homelab-api's database connection settings?
 An existing /etc/homelab/api/config.yml was found on this machine.
 homelab-api-backend-processor connects to the same PostgreSQL database
 independently — reuse the same host/port/name/user/password from that
 file instead of entering them again?

Template: homelab-api-backend-processor/db/host
Type: string
Default: localhost
Description: PostgreSQL database host:
 Enter the same PostgreSQL server homelab-api uses (this daemon connects
 independently and needs its own copy of the credentials).

Template: homelab-api-backend-processor/db/port
Type: string
Default: 5432
Description: PostgreSQL database port:

Template: homelab-api-backend-processor/db/name
Type: string
Default: mailserver
Description: PostgreSQL database name:

Template: homelab-api-backend-processor/db/user
Type: string
Default: homelab_processor
Description: PostgreSQL database username:

Template: homelab-api-backend-processor/db/password
Type: password
Description: PostgreSQL database password:
